-- title:
--   Transport of the node block along the level-field identification
-- statement:
--   **Data.** Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M') = \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)(j_{\mathsf q}, j_{\mathsf q,M'})$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and an inclusion $\mathrm{hle}$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, itself generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}_d\,j_{\mathsf q}$ for $d \mid M'$) into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M' = \mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, where $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Fix a constant reduction $R_0$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ relative to $A$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ (a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with constants $A$, a surjective residue map whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with residues of constants and with orders along a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places), and an element $s$ of $W$.
--
--   Fix further an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, elements $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$, $\ell \in \mathbb N$, $\zeta_0, \varpi_t \in k_0$, an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ cut out by $A$ (membership in $A_b$ is membership of the image in $A$) and an element $\varpi_b \in A_b$; a prime $\ell'$; $\xi \in k_0$; an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ over $k_0$, carrying an algebra structure over $A \cap k_0$ (the pullback of $A$ to $k_0$) compatible with $k_0$; a nonzero $j_\ell \in K_\ell$; $\varpi_t' \in A \cap k_0$; an ideal $y$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}(A\cap k_0, K_\ell, j_\ell)$, the subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $(A\cap k_0)[j_\ell]$; a subalgebra $B_t \subseteq K_\ell$ over $A\cap k_0$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with $B_t \subseteq W_t$; $n \in \mathbb N$, $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$, $m \in \mathbb N$, an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A\cap k_0$ at its maximal ideal, a proof $\mathrm{hjK}$ that $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,(q\ell')$ (the $j$-expansion rescaled by $\mathsf q \mapsto \mathsf q^{q\ell'}$) lies in $K_\ell$, an element $a_0 \in A\cap k_0$, a finite set $\mathrm{ends}$ of subrings of $K_\ell$, and finally a term $\mathcal F$ of the structure $\mathrm{RigidDescentHyps}$ for exactly these arguments, which bundles the standing rigidity hypotheses of the descent.
--
--   **The fixed field and its attached objects.** Let $G$ be the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ generated by those $\tau$ for which there exists $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$; the latter predicate says that for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f, g$ on $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$ with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$, with integral $q$-expansions and $g$'s expansion nonzero, all $x \in K_\ell$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $f/g$, and all $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$, one has $\iota_*(\tau x) \cdot (g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1})^{\wedge} = (f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1})^{\wedge}$ as $q$-expansions. Let $K_0 = \mathrm{fixedField}\,G$, let $B_0$ be the subalgebra of $G$-invariants of $B_t$, and let $W_0'$ be the valuation subring of $K_0$ cut out by $W_t$.
--
--   **Descent data.** $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$. The assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ characterised by the coefficient condition that $f \in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in the image of $k_0$, and for every $k_0$-algebra isomorphism $\varphi : K_0 \xrightarrow{\sim} F_0$ subject to three compatibilities: ($\varphi 1$) for all $f \in K_0$ the coefficientwise image over $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the Laurent series of $f$ equals $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}\,\ell'$ applied to the Laurent series of $\varphi f$; ($\varphi 4$) for every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), every primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity $\xi' \in k_0$ with $\zeta = \xi'^{\ell'}$, every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ satisfying $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi'\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma\,K_\ell\,\tau$, the automorphism $\tau$ maps $K_0$ into itself and $\varphi(\tau f) = \mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,(\varphi f)$ for all $f \in K_0$, where $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ is the chosen $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphism of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ satisfying $\mathrm{IsLevelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ when one exists and the identity otherwise; ($\varphi 5$) for every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field over $\mathbb Q$ such that $\mathrm{qExpand}_{k_0}\,\ell'(\mathrm{coeffEmb}_{k_0} g)$ lies in $K_\ell$ and in $K_0$, $\varphi$ sends that element to the image of $g$ under $\mathrm{hle}$. Finally, $W_0$ is the valuation subring $\varphi(W_0')$ of $F_0$ (the preimage of $W_0'$ under $\varphi^{-1}$) and $B$ is the subring of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ consisting exactly of the images under $\varphi$ of the elements of $K_0$ lying in $B_0$.
--
--   **Hypothesis (the node block upstairs).** The hypothesis is the statement displayed below as the conclusion, read over $K_0$; its clauses are, in the same order: the cardinality $q+1$ of the node set; the common finitely generated chart $B_c$ with each node a localisation of it; level-equivariance and transitivity of the nodes, here formulated with automorphisms $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ satisfying $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, transporting membership of $f \in K_0$ with $\tau f \in K_0$; pairwise separation of the nodes; the valuative cover over $s$, whose first alternative is that all of $B_0$ lies in the given valuation subring; and, for each node, domination by $W_0'$, local noetherianness, the identification of the constants with $A\cap k_0$, the constant approximation of elements modulo non-units, and the block consisting of the crossing-model data, the monomial germ of $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,(q\ell') - a_0$ for the given $a_0 \in A \cap k_0$, the Igusa branch $W_x$ with its separation clause against the other nodes, and the pole chart $B_x$, in which the pole condition is taken at the places of $K_\ell$ over $k_0$ where $j_\ell$ has nonnegative order and the distinguished element is $\mathrm{qExpand}_{k_0}\,\ell'(\mathrm{coeffEmb}_{k_0} j_{\mathsf q})$, and in which modular functions $g$ are represented by $\mathrm{qExpand}_{k_0}\,\ell'(\mathrm{coeffEmb}_{k_0} g)$. The congruence for $a_0$ is there in the conditional form: whenever the image of $a_0$ lies in $A$, its residue raised to the $q$-th power equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $\hat\jmath$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Write $\hat\jmath$ for the element of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ given by the coefficientwise image of $j_{\mathsf q}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and for $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field write $\hat g$ for the corresponding element. Then there exist: a proof that $\hat\jmath \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$; a proof that $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(\hat\jmath)$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$; a proof $\mathrm{hJK}$ that $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}\,q$ lies in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$; an element $a_0 \in k_0$ with $a_0 \in A$ and $\mathrm{residue}_A(a_0)^q = s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(\hat\jmath))$; and a finite set $\mathrm{nodes}$ of subrings of $F_0$, such that the following hold.
--
--   (i) $\mathrm{nodes}$ has exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   (ii) There is a subring $B_c \subseteq F_0$ of the form $\mathrm{Subring.closure}$ of the set of images in $F_0$ of the elements $x \in k_0$ with $x \in A$ together with a finite set $T \subseteq F_0$, such that every $O \in \mathrm{nodes}$ contains $B_c$ and, for every $f \in F_0$, $f \in O$ if and only if there are $g, h \in B_c$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h \in O$, and $fh = g$.
--
--   (iii) For every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $O \in \mathrm{nodes}$ there is $O' \in \mathrm{nodes}$ such that for all $f \in \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with $f \in F_0$ and $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f \in F_0$, one has $f \in O$ if and only if $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,f \in O'$.
--
--   (iv) For every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and all $O, O' \in \mathrm{nodes}$ there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with the same transport equivalence from $O$ to $O'$.
--
--   (v) For distinct $O, O' \in \mathrm{nodes}$ there is $f \in F_0$ lying in both, which is not a unit of $O$ and is a unit of $O'$.
--
--   (vi) For every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ whose constants are $A \cap k_0$ (for $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $V$) and which satisfies the reduction dictionary — for every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field with $\hat g \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $\hat g$ has nonnegative order at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $\hat\jmath$ has nonnegative order, and such that $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(\hat g)$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $\hat g$ under $\mathrm{hle}$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$, and for every $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ and $\mathrm{residue}_A(c) = s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(\hat g))$ the difference of that image and $c$ lies in $V$ and in the maximal ideal of $V$ — either every $f \in B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$, or there is $O \in \mathrm{nodes}$ such that every $f \in O$ lies in $V$ and every non-unit of $O$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   (vii) For every $O \in \mathrm{nodes}$: every $f \in O$ lies in $W_0$; $O$ is a local ring and a noetherian ring; for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $O$; every $f \in O$ admits $x \in k_0$ with $x \in A$ and image in $O$ such that $f - x$ is not a unit of $O$; and there exist $E_0 \in \mathbb N$ with $1 \le E_0$, a unit $v$ of $A \cap k_0$ (both $v$ and $v^{-1}$ in $A$) with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s} v$, where $\mathrm{placeWidthChar}$ is the $j$-width at $s$ in the convention depending on $q$ divided by the $j$-ramification of $s$, a proof that the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $O$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism
--   $$\iota : \widehat{O} \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } \widehat{A\cap k_0}[\![U,V]\!]/(UV - \pi_0^{E_0})$$
--   from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model over the adic completion of $A \cap k_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that crossing model, such that:
--
--   (a) $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$;
--
--   (b) $\iota$ carries the image of every constant $x \in k_0$ with $x \in A$ and image in $O$ to $\mathrm{const}(x)$;
--
--   (c) $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$;
--
--   (d) $c_y \in W_0$ and lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, while $c_x$, whenever it lies in $W_0$, is not in the maximal ideal of $W_0$;
--
--   (e) (monomial germ) there are a proof that $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}\,q$ minus the image of $a_0$ lies in $F_0$, a proof that this element lies in $O$, an integer $e \ge 1$ and a unit $w_V$ of the crossing model with $\iota$ of that element equal to $w_V \cdot V^e$;
--
--   (f) (Igusa branch) there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, with constants $A \cap k_0$, which is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$; there is $t \in W_x$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then so does every coefficient of $p$; $c_x$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and $c_y$ does not; for every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field with $\hat g \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and with nonnegative order at every place where $\hat\jmath$ has nonnegative order, the image of $\hat g$ under $\mathrm{hle}$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ if and only if $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(\hat g) = 0$, and, if $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(\hat g)$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lies in $O$ and is, after subtraction of any constant $c \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\mathrm{residue}_A(c) = s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(\hat g))$, a non-unit of $O$; and for every other node $O' \ne O$ there is $f \in O'$ with $f \notin W_x$;
--
--   (g) (pole chart) there is a subring $B_x \subseteq F_0$ such that every $f \in B_x$ lies in $B$ and in $O$; every $f \in B_x$ has nonnegative order at every place of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of $\hat\jmath$ under $\mathrm{hle}$ has nonnegative order; for $f \in F_0$, $f \in O$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h \in O$; every $f \in F_0$ is such a quotient with $g, h \in B_x$ and $h \ne 0$; $B_x$ is the subring generated by the images of the elements of $A \cap k_0$ together with a finite set $T \subseteq F_0$; and there is $b \in B_x$ such that for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with constants $A \cap k_0$, with the image of $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal of $V$, such that the image of $\hat\jmath$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$ and $p(\hat\jmath)$ avoids the maximal ideal of $V$ for every monic polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$, and such that some $f \in O$ lies outside $V$, one has $b \notin V$.
--
--   This is the transport step in the semistable analysis of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$: the block of local data at the $q+1$ nodes of the fibre over $s$ — common chart, level-equivariance, valuative cover, crossing-model germ of the modular invariant, Igusa branch and pole chart — is carried from the auxiliary field $K_0 \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ of level $q\ell'$ across the isomorphism $\varphi$ onto the level-$q$ field $F_0$. It is cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart).
